  "preview": "The moment you become a parent, everyone suddenly becomes an expert. You should sleep train. Never sleep train. Feed this way. Definitely not that way. Buy this. Avoid that. Oookaaay. Byeeee! The same",
  "text": "The moment you become a parent, everyone suddenly becomes an expert.\n\nYou should sleep train.\nNever sleep train.\nFeed this way.\nDefinitely not that way.\nBuy this.\nAvoid that.\n\nOookaaay. Byeeee!\n\nThe same goes for design. Show a concept to ten people, and you'll get twelve opinions.\n\nAnd even though it's hard to believe at first — most of the feedback comes from a good place. People care, they really do. Let's just agree on that, okay? Okay.\n\nWell, the real challenge is learning how to listen without losing your own… vision. Aha.\n\nI've learned that not every opinion deserves equal weight — but every opinion deserves to be understood (except people we don't like, ooopsie). Sometimes feedback reveals a real problem, sometimes a personal preference. But seriously, knowing the difference is half the job.\n\nEither way — whether in design or in parenting — the most important thing is to listen and trust yourself. Easier said than done when your self-confidence is running at, let's say, a 4 out of 10 on a good day. But I'm working on it. Hard. And I hope you are too.\n\nSo, navigating a world where everyone has the definitive answer on how to raise your baby and how to design your product?\n\nDivas, let's talk. 🙈\n\n\n#Design \n#AI \n#UXDesign \n#Creativity \n#Feedback \n#ClaudeAI \n#ProductDesign",
